<HelloFraandsPage title="Recording & AI safety" summary="Hum call record nahi karte. AI live dhyaan rakhta hai." review={true} related={[{href:'/privacy',label:'Privacy policy'},{href:'/faq#ai-safety',label:'AI safety FAQs'},{href:'/grievance',label:'Grievance redressal'}]}>
<h2>We do not record calls</h2>
<p>{BRAND.name} does not record calls and does not store call audio. There is no recording to download, share, leak or listen to later — for you, for the other person or for us.</p>
<h2>No human listens</h2>
<p>No person at {BRAND.name} monitors or listens to live calls. We are a switch: our system rings the host, and once the host accepts it rings the caller and joins the two calls through a platform number, so neither person sees the other's number.</p>
<h2>How AI keeps the call safe</h2>
<p>While a call is live, our AI follows the conversation in real time. It does not react to single words or keyword lists — it understands the <strong>intention</strong> of the caller. If it detects harassment, abuse, threats, sexual pressure, or a scam such as asking for an OTP, UPI PIN, card or bank details, it ends the call automatically and flags the account.</p>
<p>The AI looks at the conversation as it happens and does not keep a recording. In the women-only space it is tuned to recognise ordinary health and intimate-wellness discussion, so describing a symptom or a bad experience is not treated as misconduct. A mention of self-harm is never a strike.</p>
<h2>What we keep about a call</h2>
<p>Only the records needed to run the service, bill fairly and handle complaints: the participants (as account IDs), connection and end times, duration, rate, charge, and whether the call was ended by a person or by a safety action. No audio, no transcript.</p>
<h2>Strikes and reviews</h2>
<p>An AI safety action ends the call and creates a flag. Our trust &amp; safety team reviews flags and reports before confirming a strike; three confirmed strikes means a permanent ban, and serious cases such as threats, sexual harassment or fraud can be banned straight away. If you think a call was ended or an account restricted unfairly, use <a href="/grievance">grievance redressal</a>.</p>
<h2>Your part</h2>
<p>Either person can hang up at any time, and pressing <strong>#</strong> ends the call and blocks the other person. Do not make your own recording of the other person — it breaks the <a href="/community-guidelines">community guidelines</a>. Number masking hides your number, not what you say, so keep your address, workplace, social accounts, OTPs and bank details to yourself.</p>
</HelloFraandsPage>
